Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||03-21-2001||06:50 PM||||Here's a showcase of my cars...<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high"> <BR>1988 GT - Red/Beechwood<BR>Factory options: T-top, Leather seats, Spoiler, AC, rear def, PW, PL, PM, 5-spd Getrag, tilt, passenger vanity mirror.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402882&Sequence=1&res=high"> <BR>1987 SE - Med Red Metallic/Grey<BR>Factory options: Sunroof, Spoiler, AC, 5-spd Isuzu, tilt, Subwoofer/Performance Sound, manual windows, manual locks, manual mirrors, no rear def.<P>Non-Factory options: 86-87 GT 15 inch grey rims, Holley side scoop.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402876&Sequence=1&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402878&Sequence=1&res=high"> <P>These are the reasons I love Fieros soooo much... They are fun to restore/maintain and look great even among today's two-seat sport coupes.<P>Kelvin Vivian||||reg||1
